WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.287
The new kittens were soon hidden safely with the others, thanks to Sebastian.

2
00:00:05.288 --> 00:00:11.509
For the second day now, Clara's lesson had been interrupted with laughter and excitement.

3
00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:15.995
Later in the day, everything was explained to Fraulein.

4
00:00:15.996 --> 00:00:22.495
She quickly realized that Heidi's trip the day before was the cause of all the chaos.

5
00:00:22.496 --> 00:00:28.191
"I am going to punish you for all your bad behavior," she told Heidi.

6
00:00:28.192 --> 00:00:32.651
"I'll put you in the cellar with the rats and black beetles."

7
00:00:32.652 --> 00:00:34.930
Heidi was silent and puzzled.

8
00:00:34.931 --> 00:00:41.027
She did not know what a cellar was like, and she had never seen a rat or a black beetle.

9
00:00:41.028 --> 00:00:44.554
But Clara interrupted in great distress.

10
00:00:44.555 --> 00:00:49.928
Clara's father had written to say that he would be home soon, so she said,

11
00:00:49.929 --> 00:00:54.285
"No, no, Fraulein, you must wait until Father arrives.

12
00:00:54.286 --> 00:00:57.073
He will say what is to be done with Heidi."

13
00:00:57.074 --> 00:01:05.558
"Fine, Clara, but I will have something to say to Herr Sesemann when he arrives!" replied Fraulein.

14
00:01:05.559 --> 00:01:09.340
The next days went by without any further disturbance.

15
00:01:09.341 --> 00:01:12.301
Heidi and Clara did their lessons in the mornings.

16
00:01:12.302 --> 00:01:22.218
In the afternoons, Heidi told Clara about Grandfather's hut on the mountain, about Peter and the goats, and Peter's Grannie.

17
00:01:22.219 --> 00:01:25.113
Heidi's heart was longing to return.

18
00:01:25.114 --> 00:01:27.676
She would always finish her stories with,

19
00:01:27.677 --> 00:01:29.359
"I must go home!

20
00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:33.169
Tomorrow I must really go home!"

21
00:01:33.170 --> 00:01:39.327
Even though Heidi missed her old home, she had a secret that cheered her up a little every day.

22
00:01:39.328 --> 00:01:45.725
She knew how much Peter's grandmother would love the soft white rolls that were served with dinner.

23
00:01:45.726 --> 00:01:52.366
So after each meal, she pocketed a roll and saved it in her room.

24
00:01:52.367 --> 00:02:00.762
Detie had told her that she could go home any time she wanted, and one morning Heidi decided she could stay no longer.

25
00:02:00.763 --> 00:02:08.557
From the bundle of clothes Detie had brought to Frankfurt, Heidi chose her red shawl and straw hat.

26
00:02:08.558 --> 00:02:13.511
She tied up the rolls in her shawl and put the hat on her head.

27
00:02:13.512 --> 00:02:17.620
Just as she reached the front door, she ran into Fraulein.

28
00:02:17.621 --> 00:02:19.795
"What are you doing?

29
00:02:19.796 --> 00:02:25.007
Have I not strictly forbidden you to run about?" said Fraulein.

30
00:02:25.008 --> 00:02:27.182
"I am not going to run about.

31
00:02:27.183 --> 00:02:28.646
I am going home!"

32
00:02:28.647 --> 00:02:32.463
said Heidi, hiding the bundle of rolls behind her back.

33
00:02:32.464 --> 00:02:34.434
"What are you talking about?

34
00:02:34.435 --> 00:02:36.820
Have you not been treated well here?

35
00:02:36.821 --> 00:02:41.220
What would Clara's father say?" said Fraulein.

36
00:02:41.221 --> 00:02:43.607
"But I only want to go home.

37
00:02:43.608 --> 00:02:45.681
Grannie is waiting for me.

38
00:02:45.682 --> 00:02:47.943
I can't share my lunch with Peter.

39
00:02:47.944 --> 00:02:52.571
And I can't watch the sunset on the mountains!" exclaimed Heidi.

40
00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:57.572
"The child is out of her mind!" cried Fraulein.

41
00:02:57.573 --> 00:03:03.298
She grabbed Heidi's hand, took away her hat and shawl, and gave them to Sebastian.

42
00:03:03.299 --> 00:03:07.392
"Take her to her room at once," said Fraulein.

43
00:03:07.393 --> 00:03:11.057
Heidi climbed the stairs with slow, heavy steps.

44
00:03:11.058 --> 00:03:13.913
Sebastian felt sad as he watched her.

45
00:03:13.914 --> 00:03:16.111
"Don't give in!" he said.

46
00:03:16.112 --> 00:03:18.160
"Don't let her make you unhappy!

47
00:03:18.161 --> 00:03:20.333
Keep up your courage!"

48
00:03:20.334 --> 00:03:26.868
Later in the day, Fraulein remembered what Heidi had been wearing when she had tried to leave.

49
00:03:26.869 --> 00:03:30.846
She decided to add some of Clara's clothes to Heidi's wardrobe.

50
00:03:30.847 --> 00:03:36.104
When she opened Heidi's closet, she couldn't believe what she saw.

51
00:03:36.105 --> 00:03:38.420
"What is this, Heidi?

52
00:03:38.421 --> 00:03:42.328
A pile of old rolls in the bottom of your closet?!"

53
00:03:42.329 --> 00:03:44.377
Fraulein called Sebastian.

54
00:03:44.378 --> 00:03:49.132
"Take away these old rolls at once!" ordered Fraulein.

55
00:03:49.133 --> 00:03:55.242
"No, no!" screamed Heidi. "The rolls are for Grannie!"

56
00:03:55.243 --> 00:04:03.015
But Fraulein would not listen, and Heidi flung herself down on her bed in despair.

